---
layout: layout.njk
title: "Diseases We Treat | CoreFlow Specialty Infusion | South Carolina"
description: "Conditions prescribers ask us about, by name or specialty. Call CoreFlow Specialty Infusion to confirm we can service a referral before you send it."
ogTitle: "Diseases We Treat | CoreFlow Specialty Infusion"
ogDescription: "Browse conditions by name or specialty, and call to confirm before you refer."
activeNav: diseases
permalink: "/diseases-we-treat.html"
pageScript: "finder.js"
robots: "noindex, nofollow"
---
{#- Every condition rendered here comes from _data/conditions.json. Nothing on
    this page hardcodes a condition name — verify-coreflow Check 17 enforces it.

    NOTE FOR WHOEVER EDITS THIS NEXT: the condition list is a SEED, not a service
    claim, pending Greg's confirmed list. Three reviewers blocked an earlier draft
    for reading as settled, so the service framing is deliberately absent: the
    page-level notice sits inside the hero above the list, the description says "ask us
    about" rather than "supports", and every per-condition action is a phone call
    to confirm — NOT a one-click referral.

    `robots: noindex, nofollow` is set and the page is absent from sitemap.xml, but
    do NOT over-trust that: this page is linked from the primary nav and the footer
    on every page, so noindex holds back crawlers and nothing else. The on-page
    framing is what actually protects a human visitor.

    WHEN GREG'S LIST LANDS and every entry in _data/conditions.json reads
    status "confirmed": delete the .note-box--review block, restore the
    per-condition referral CTA, drop the robots line, and add the page to
    sitemap.xml — in one commit. See docs/stage2/blockers.md. -#}
{%- set conditionList = conditions.conditions -%}
{%- set specialties = therapies.specialties -%}

<section class="hero">
 <div class="container">
 <span class="hero__eyebrow">For Prescribers &amp; Office Staff</span>
 <h1 class="hero__title">Diseases we treat</h1>

 {#- The notice sits above the CTAs on purpose: a prescriber must meet the
     caveat before the list, not one section below it. -#}
 <div class="note-box note-box--review">
  <p><strong>This list is under clinical review and is not final.</strong> These are the
  conditions prescribers ask us about most &mdash; not a settled list of what we can service.
  Call <a href="tel:{{ site.phoneTel }}">{{ site.phone }}</a> with the diagnosis and the therapy
  and we'll tell you before you send anything. If you already know the therapy,
  <a href="drugs-we-provide.html">search the drugs we provide</a> instead.</p>
 </div>

 {% include "physician-order-notice.njk" %}
 </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight" data-finder data-finder-noun="conditions">
 <div class="container">

  <form class="finder__controls" data-finder-controls data-finder-form hidden>
   <div class="finder__field">
    <label class="finder__label" for="condition-search">Search conditions</label>
    <input class="finder__input" id="condition-search" type="search" autocomplete="off"
           placeholder="Condition, abbreviation, or specialty"
           aria-describedby="condition-search-hint"
           data-finder-input>
    <p class="finder__hint" id="condition-search-hint">Matches full condition names, the common abbreviations for them, and specialties.</p>
   </div>
   <button class="btn btn--secondary finder__clear" type="button" data-finder-clear disabled>Clear search</button>
  </form>

  {#- Chips target real per-specialty anchors so they still do something useful
      without JS; with JS they filter in place instead of scrolling. -#}
  <nav class="finder__chips" aria-label="Filter by specialty">
   <ul class="finder__chip-list" role="list">
   {%- for specialty in specialties %}
    <li><a class="finder__chip" href="#condition-{{ specialty.id }}" data-finder-filter="{{ specialty.id }}">{{ specialty.name }}</a></li>
   {%- endfor %}
   </ul>
  </nav>

  <p class="finder__status" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-finder-status>Showing all {{ conditionList | length }} conditions, grouped by specialty.</p>

  <div class="note-box note-box--empty container--narrow text-center" hidden data-finder-empty>
   <p><strong>No match on this page &mdash; and that is not the same as no.</strong>
   Give us the diagnosis and the prescribed therapy and we'll tell you whether we can
   service the referral before you send anything.</p>
   <p><a class="btn btn--primary" href="tel:{{ site.phoneTel }}">Call {{ site.phone }} →</a></p>
  </div>

  {%- for specialty in specialties %}
  {%- set inSpecialty = conditionList | inSpecialty(specialty.id) %}
  <section class="finder__group" id="condition-{{ specialty.id }}" data-finder-group="{{ specialty.id }}">
   <h2 class="section-title section-title--group">{{ specialty.name }}</h2>
   {%- if inSpecialty | length %}
   <ul class="condition-list" role="list">
   {%- for condition in inSpecialty %}
    <li class="condition" data-finder-item data-finder-key="{{ condition.name }}"
        data-specialties="{{ condition.specialties | join(' ') }}"
        data-search="{{ condition.name }} {{ condition.full }} {{ condition.aliases | join(' ') }} {{ condition.specialties | specialtyNames(specialties) | join(' ') }}">
     <h3 class="condition__name">{{ condition.name }}</h3>
     {%- if condition.full %}<p class="condition__full">{{ condition.full }}</p>{% endif %}
     <p class="condition__tags"><span class="visually-hidden">Specialties: </span>
     {%- for name in condition.specialties | specialtyNames(specialties) %}
      <span class="condition__tag">{{ name }}</span>
     {%- endfor %}
     </p>
     {#- Deliberately a phone call, not a referral link: nothing on this page is
         confirmed, so a one-click referral would be the exact failure the notice
         above warns about. Restore the referral CTA when Greg signs the list off. -#}
     <p class="condition__action"><a href="https://coreflowrx.com/refer#referral-form">Start a referral for {{ condition.name }} →</a></p>
    </li>
   {%- endfor %}
   </ul>
   {%- else %}
   {#- Mirrors the empty-specialty block on /drugs-we-provide so the two sibling
       pages answer the same click the same way. -#}
   <div class="card card--soft finder__pending">
    <p><strong>No {{ specialty.name | lower }} conditions listed yet.</strong>
    This list is still being confirmed with our clinical team. Tell us the diagnosis
    and the prescribed therapy and we'll answer straight away.</p>
    <p><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="tel:{{ site.phoneTel }}">Call {{ site.phone }} →</a></p>
   </div>
   {%- endif %}
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

 </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--soft">
 <div class="container">
  <h2 class="section-title">Don't see the diagnosis?</h2>
  <p class="lead">Call us before you decide we can't help. We would rather answer the question
  in a quick phone call than have you route the patient elsewhere by default.</p>
  <div class="grid grid--3 mt-6">
   <div class="card"><h3>Call and ask</h3><p><strong>{{ site.phone }}</strong><br>{{ site.hours }}</p><p>Give us the diagnosis and the prescribed therapy and we'll confirm whether we can service it.</p><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="tel:{{ site.phoneTel }}">Call now →</a></div>
   <div class="card"><h3>Start from the drug</h3><p>If you already know the therapy, searching the confirmed drug list is the faster route.</p><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="drugs-we-provide.html">Drugs We Provide →</a></div>
   <div class="card"><h3>Send a referral</h3><p>Once we've confirmed we can service it: online through our BAA-covered form, or by fax.</p><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="refer.html">Refer a Patient →</a></div>
  </div>
  <p class="footnote mt-4"><em>All therapies are subject to formulary availability, clinical suitability, and payer authorization. Listing a condition on this page does not mean a particular referral can be serviced &mdash; we confirm case by case.</em></p>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
 <div class="container">
  {% include "referral-checklist.njk" %}
 </div>
</section>
